Cmn10=display power or whatever conditions should determine the system||1
Cmn11=is in an "on" state\\System Power Off Pulse\\a pulsed signal that||1
Cmn12=fires when the system has turned off\\System Power Off Fb\\a latching||1
Cmn13=signal that is used when the online signal changes, to force the||1
Cmn14=interface to the splash page\\System Power On Fb\\a latching signal||1
Cmn15=that is used when the online signal changes, to force the interface||1
Cmn16=to the main page\\Request Splash Page\\pulse this to have the interface||1
Cmn17=show the splash page\\this signal can be looped with the System||1
Cmn18=Power Off OS output signal to make sure that the panel will go back||1
Cmn19=to the splash page no matter which panel request a system shutdown\\
Cmn20=Request Main Page\\pulse this to have the interface show the main||1
Cmn21=page\\this will also cause the Modal Page Fb to change to the value||1
Cmn22=of Default Modal Page\\Modal Page\\requests the user interface to||1
Cmn23=show the modal page\\Show System Off Confirmation Page\\request||1
Cmn24=that the interface shows the system off confirmation page\\hides||1
Cmn25=any modal pages, by setting Modal Page Fb to zero\\Hide System Off||1
Cmn26=Confirmation Page\\hides the system off confirmation page\\recalls||1
Cmn27=the last value that Modal Page was set to\\Outputs\\System Power||1
Cmn28=Off OS\\this should be a jammed signal that all touchpanels output||1
Cmn29=to force them to all stay in sync, and cause the system to turn||1
Cmn30=off no matter what panel requests it\\Show Splash Page Fb\\a digital||1
Cmn31=signal that will go high when the splash page should be shown\\Show||1
Cmn32=Main Page Fb\\a digital signal that will go high whe the main page||1
Cmn33=should be shown\\Modal Page Fb\\this should be routed to an analog||1
Cmn34=equate to show modal subpages as needed\\this will automatically||1
